   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the resilience  in 4 communities in Masisi/North Kivu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at contributing to a sustainable capacity building of civil society to claim and access their rights to life and security, by actively participating in decisions that affect them, and by fostering relationships with local authorities who will be informed of their obligations in terms of protection and livelihoods. Implementation Approach will be mainly focusing on: Community Based Protection (CBP) with the Community Protection Structure (SPC); capacity building initiatives for Farmers&apos; Organizations, community members and local authorities,  on production and marketing of agricultural products, on Local Humanitarian Leadership (LHL) on peaceful conflict resolution. The project direct beneficiaries target is 12000, it will be implemented in partnership with local Non Governmental Organisations (NGOs) in four new communities in Masisi territory</narrative>
  </description>
